          %h2#aks_primality_test AKS primality test
          %p
            A generalization of Fermat’s little theorem can be used to give a deterministic test for primality that can be carried out on any integer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            in “polynomial time” (bounded by a polynomial applied to the number of digits of
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              An integer
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
              is prime if and only if
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≡
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace"} (
                      %mo{:rspace => "thinmathspace"} mod
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:rspace => "mediummathspace"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-a)^n \equiv x^n - a \pmod{n}
            %p
              for every or even any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              coprime to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (so that, for example, the case
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a=1
              would be a sufficient criterion for primality).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "nlab/show/freshman's+dream#primality"} argument at freshman’s dream
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is equivalent to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≡
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace"} (
                      %mo{:rspace => "thinmathspace"} mod
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:rspace => "mediummathspace"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x-a)^n \equiv x^n - a^n \pmod{n}
              (for every or any
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
